    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Given four positive integers \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) that leave remainders of 2, 4, 6, and 8 respectively when divided by 11, we can express these integers as:\n\\[ a = 11k + 2, \\]\n\\[ b = 11m + 4, \\]\n\\[ c = 11n + 6, \\]\n\\[ d = 11p + 8, \\]\nfor some integers \\(k\\), \\(m\\), \\(n\\), and \\(p\\).\n\nThe sum of these integers \\(a + b + c + d\\) is:\n\\[ a + b + c + d = (11k + 2) + (11m + 4) + (11n + 6) + (11p + 8) = 11(k + m + n + p) + 20. \\]\n\nWhen this sum is divided by 11, the term \\(11(k + m + n + p)\\) is divisible by 11, and thus it contributes 0 to the remainder. Therefore, the remainder when \\(a + b + c + d\\) is divided by 11 is the same as the remainder when 20 is divided by 11. We find:\n\\[ 20 \\div 11 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 9, \\]\nso the remainder is:\n\\[ 20 \\equiv 9 \\pmod{11}. \\]\n\nThus, the remainder when the sum of the four integers is divided by 11 is \\(\\boxed{9}\\).",
