      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Given four positive integers \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) such that when each is divided by 11, the remainders are 2, 4, 6, and 8 respectively. We can express these integers as:\n\\[ a = 11k + 2, \\quad b = 11m + 4, \\quad c = 11n + 6, \\quad d = 11p + 8 \\]\nfor some integers \\(k\\), \\(m\\), \\(n\\), and \\(p\\).\n\nWe need to find the remainder when the sum of these integers is divided by 11. First, we calculate the sum:\n\\[ a + b + c + d = (11k + 2) + (11m + 4) + (11n + 6) + (11p + 8) \\]\n\\[ = 11k + 11m + 11n + 11p + 2 + 4 + 6 + 8 \\]\n\\[ = 11(k + m + n + p) + 20 \\]\n\nNext, we need to find the remainder when 20 is divided by 11:\n\\[ 20 \\div 11 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 9 \\]\nThus,\n\\[ 20 \\equiv 9 \\pmod{11} \\]\nSo,\n\\[ 11(k + m + n + p) + 20 \\equiv 11(k + m + n + p) + 9 \\pmod{11} \\]\nSince \\(11(k + m + n + p)\\) is a multiple of 11 and thus leaves a remainder of 0 when divided by 11, we have:\n\\[ 11(k + m + n + p) + 9 \\equiv 9 \\pmod{11} \\]\n\nTherefore, the remainder when the sum of the four integers is divided by 11 is \\(\\boxed{9}\\).",
